# Repo-wide rules. medas-api/.gitignore and medas-ui/.gitignore each cover what
# their own toolchain produces (uv and Python output; node_modules and .next).
# This file covers what neither owns: secrets, machine and editor cruft, and
# tool caches that can appear anywhere in the tree.

# Secrets. Both packages ignore their own .env; this catches one written at the
# root, and the dotenv variants. A checked-in template stays visible.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and IDE state.
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# OS metadata. Desktop.ini and Thumbs.db come from Windows Explorer, .DS_Store
# from Finder - either can land in any directory.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Python caches. medas-api ignores __pycache__ and build output, but not the
# test and linter caches, which are written at whatever directory the tool is
# invoked from - the repo root included.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node, for a dev server or tool run from the root rather than inside medas-ui.
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
